# **Section 5: Digital Skills Assessment Tools**

Three complementary assessment tools form the baseline and ongoing measurement strategy for digital skills development across staff and learners. Each serves a distinct purpose and audience. Together they provide the before, during, and after evidence that the coaching strategy needs.

## **Jisc Building Digital Capability Discovery Tool**

The Discovery Tool is the primary baseline assessment for both staff and learners. It is free for Jisc subscribing institutions, takes approximately 20 minutes to complete, and produces a personal digital capability profile across six dimensions: information, data, and media literacy; digital creation, problem solving, and innovation; communication, collaboration, and participation; digital learning and development; ICT proficiency; and digital identity and wellbeing.

For staff, the Discovery Tool provides the baseline that coaching conversations are built on. For learners, it will be deployed in Weeks 1 and 2 of September 2026 as a standard part of induction across all curriculum areas. Results are reviewed at mid-year and end of year to track progression.

The tool has role-specific question sets for FE teaching staff, general staff, new students, current students, and employability skills. The Digital Pedagogy Coach deploys the appropriate set for each audience and reviews anonymised organisational data through the institutional dashboard.

| **How to access the Jisc Discovery Tool** Staff access the tool via the Jisc Building Digital Capability service, which Weston College subscribes to as a Jisc member. The tool produces a personal profile and a shareable link. Staff share their profile link with their TLAM or the Digital Pedagogy Coach at the start of a development conversation. Learner profiles are managed through the institutional account. Contact the Digital Pedagogy Coach for access details. Direct access: jisc.potential.ly/signin |
| --- |

[Jisc Building Digital Capability and Discovery Tool: digitalcapability.jisc.ac.uk](https://digitalcapability.jisc.ac.uk/)

## **ETF Digital Teaching Professional Framework Self-Assessment**

The ETF DTPF self-assessment tool supports staff in mapping their own teaching digital skills practice to the four stages of the framework, Exploring through to Leading. It is available via the ETF professional development platform and is free to all FE sector staff. It produces a personal development profile that maps to the Digital Learning Pyramid stages in this document.

The Digital Pedagogy Coach uses the DTPF profile as the starting point for any structured coaching conversation with a staff member about their teaching practice. It is not a judgement tool. It is a development conversation tool. The DTPF self-assessment is used alongside, not instead of, the Jisc Discovery Tool — where the Jisc tool captures the breadth of digital capability, the DTPF captures the depth of teaching-specific digital practice.

Note: ETF and SET are merging into a single MyETF platform launched 1 April 2026. Access all ETF resources via etfoundation.co.uk/professional-development using a free ETF account.

[ETF Professional Development Platform: etfoundation.co.uk/professional-development](https://etfoundation.co.uk/professional-development/)

## **Century Tech Digital Skills Initial Assessment and Diagnostics**

Century Tech is an AI-powered learning platform with a specific digital skills initial assessment and diagnostic tool. The Digital Pedagogy Coach proposes to use Century for three purposes: an initial digital skills assessment at the start of the year to establish a baseline beyond what the Jisc Discovery Tool captures; Level 1 and Entry Level 3 diagnostic themes used throughout the year to track progression at specific qualification levels; and a channel for directing staff and learner learning toward structured, assessed digital skills content.

The Century platform uses adaptive learning pathways that respond to each learner's responses, meaning the diagnostic experience is personalised rather than a fixed set of questions. This makes it particularly valuable for ESOL learners and learners with varying prior experience, where a one-size approach would be misleading.

| **Century and the Jisc Discovery Tool: the relationship** The Jisc Discovery Tool measures self-perceived digital capability across six broad dimensions. Century provides a more granular, assessed measurement of actual digital skills performance at specific qualification levels. The two tools complement each other. Discovery Tool for orientation and strategic planning. Century for specific level tracking and progression evidence. Together they give the most complete picture of where learners and staff actually are. |
| --- |

[Century Tech: century.tech](https://www.century.tech/)

