## **Pathway 2: Teachers — Digital Skills and Digital TLA Pedagogy**

This pathway covers both dimensions of Teacher Digital Skills: the personal digital competencies staff need to work effectively in a digital organisation, and the pedagogical capabilities that translate personal competence into high quality, inclusive teaching. It maps directly to the ETF Digital Teaching Professional Framework (DTPF) stages and the four stages of the Digital Learning Pyramid. The Jisc Building Digital Capability Discovery Tool (Teaching Staff question set) provides the baseline and mid-year review.

| **Starting point for staff** All new teaching staff complete the Jisc Discovery Tool Teaching Staff question set in their first half-term. Existing staff are invited to complete it at the start of each academic year. The TLAM or Digital Pedagogy Coach reviews personalised reports in a one-to-one coaching conversation. The ETF DTPF self-assessment complements this by mapping specifically to pedagogical practice stages. Both tools are accessed through institutional accounts. |
| --- |

