## **Pathway 3: General Digital Skills — All Staff**

This pathway is for all staff, teaching and non-teaching, from early career to senior leadership. It focuses on the personal and professional digital skills that everyone in the organisation needs to work effectively, securely, and confidently in a digital environment. It does not assume a teaching context. The Jisc Building Digital Capability Discovery Tool (general staff question set) provides the baseline.

| **Who this pathway is for** Support staff, administrators, curriculum managers, quality professionals, heads of area, and leaders. Anyone who has not already followed the Teacher pathway but who needs to develop their personal digital capability for their role. The four stages map directly to the Digital Learning Pyramid: Beginner and Developing sit within Digital Foundations, Embedding within Digital Inclusion, Innovating within Digital Innovation. |
| --- |

